A||||8||Ted||Washing the engine
Z||000000||Ted||07-04-99||08:18 AM||||<br>I noticed u guys were talking about washing the engine and I was wondering how I could go about doing that without any problems?
Z||000001||Racer 1||07-04-99||06:04 PM||||Wash engine when cold with light mists of  simple green.Then hose it off with light mists of water.Then if you have a airtank blow dry it off.Never take you car to the car wash and wash it with the high pressure hoses youll ruin your engine in no time!!!
Z||000002||theogre||07-05-99||10:03 PM||||Using a pressure washer can be done. You just have to be carefull where you point that thing. Dirrect, close up, spraying of someparts is a definate NoNo.
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||07-05-99||10:24 PM||||Racer 1 you get the prize. My engine was clean to start with but I live by that simple green, most of the time it can be used as a wipe down/off without the hose or pressure washer, just a wet rag & a tooth bursh and a little time, but covering dist, some elect. parts etc. with a plastic bag will help, Light mist was a good tip. Goog one Org, NO HARD SPRAY OR CLOSE UP SPRAY
Z||000004||four50four||07-06-99||02:59 PM||||i don't know about car engines ( i usually just give mine a wipe down with a wet rag) but i know for dirt bikes pressure washing destroys them if you get close to the motor. i suggest not to get any pressure washer close to your motor.
Z||000005||PaUL||07-07-99||07:31 PM||||Ive used both simple green and specialized "foaming" engine cleaners to wash my engine. Both seem to work well but you get more washes with the simple green.
Z||000006||Carrolles||07-08-99||11:17 AM||||I use SuperClean.  It is like Simple Green but more concentrated.  I secure a plastic drop cloth over the trunk opening with bungee cords and spray down everything with SuperClean.  Having the engine warm helps.  I use a parts cleaning brush to get at thick stuff, wait a few minutes and hose it off.  I've never had a problem with this method on any of my cars for the past 25 years. <br>Obviously it isn't wise to spray hard directly on the distributor or altenator but I don't take extreme measures to not hit them with hte hose.  Start the engine right after cleaning to dry it off. 
Z||000007||PaUL||07-08-99||02:10 PM||||Is that SuperClean from Castrol?
Z||000008||BN Boomer||07-08-99||02:51 PM||||I've used Simple Green to clean dirtbikes and automobile engines for years. I buy it at PriceCostco for $7.99 for for a 140oz jug. Best price I've seen anywhere. I also bought a toilet cleaning brush to use for scrubbing the engines and whatnot. They're inexpensive and you'd be surprised the nooks and crannies they will get into. The only thing I take any care not to spray the Simple Green on is the alternator. 
